---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Stellar Populations Cheat Sheet | Free Pop I, Pop II, Pop III"
  description="Complete stellar populations cheat sheet with Pop I, Pop II, and Pop III stars. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Stellar Populations<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Pop I, Pop II, and Pop III stars. From metal-rich to metal-free stars.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Population Classification</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Population I (Pop I)</h3>
        <pre><code>Metal-rich: Z ~ 0.02 (2% metals)
Found in: spiral arms, disk
Young stars: age < 10 Gyr
Examples: Sun, most visible stars
Formation: from enriched ISM</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Population II (Pop II)</h3>
        <pre><code>Metal-poor: Z ~ 0.001 (0.1% metals)
Found in: halo, globular clusters
Old stars: age > 10 Gyr
Examples: stars in globular clusters
Formation: from primordial gas</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Population III (Pop III)</h3>
        <pre><code>Metal-free: Z = 0
First stars in universe
Massive: M > 100 M_sun
Short-lived: < 1 Myr
No direct observations yet</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Metallicity Effects</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Stellar Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Higher Z: cooler, redder, more opaque
Lower Z: hotter, bluer, more transparent
Metal lines: absorption features in spectra
Mass loss: higher Z → stronger winds
Evolution: Z affects all stages</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Age Determination</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Methods</h3>
        <pre><code>Isochrone fitting: HR diagram position
Main sequence turnoff: oldest main-sequence star
White dwarf cooling: age of stellar population
Nucleocosmochronology: radioactive dating
Lithium depletion: lithium abundance</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
